    {
      "_comment": "listPlatformUsers (change: admin-user-activity-dashboard) runs an EQUALITY-ONLY collection-group query: collectionGroup('runs').where('ownerUid','==',uid). Firestore does NOT auto-index single fields at COLLECTION_GROUP scope, and the (ownerUid, status) composite above does not satisfy it either — production answered this exact query with FAILED_PRECONDITION asking for COLLECTION_GROUP_ASC on runs.ownerUid. Deploy indexes BEFORE the functions that use them.",
      "collectionGroup": "runs",
      "fieldPath": "ownerUid",
      "indexes": [
        { "order": "ASCENDING", "queryScope": "COLLECTION" },
        { "order": "ASCENDING", "queryScope": "COLLECTION_GROUP" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_comment": "listGameTemplates / createGameFromTemplate (change: admin-manage-game-templates) run an EQUALITY-ONLY collection-group query: collectionGroup('games').where('isTemplate','==',true), and listAdminTemplates runs the same equality at COLLECTION scope: collection('users/{uid}/games').where('isTemplate','==',true). BOTH scopes must be listed. A fieldOverrides entry REPLACES Firestore's automatic single-field indexing for that field — it does not add to it — so declaring COLLECTION_GROUP alone silently DISABLED the ordinary collection index that had been automatic, and listAdminTemplates answered every call with FAILED_PRECONDITION while the collection-group query kept working. That reads exactly like \"the templates tab is broken but the creator picker still shows my templates\": the admin console showed a load error and offered no Edit button, while every creator kept seeing the same templates in the new-game picker. Grouping/sorting happens in application code, so only the equality filter needs an index, not a composite with templateOrder. Deploy BEFORE the functions that use it.",
      "collectionGroup": "games",
      "fieldPath": "isTemplate",
      "indexes": [
        { "order": "ASCENDING", "queryScope": "COLLECTION" },
        { "order": "ASCENDING", "queryScope": "COLLECTION_GROUP" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
